.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.TH fleetring-agent-delegate 1  FleetRing "FleetRing manual"
.SH NAME
fleetring\-agent\-delegate \- Asks the control plane for a delegated agent\*(Aqs token, as its parent
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBfleetring agent delegate\fR [\fB\-\-scope\fR] [\fB\-\-ttl\fR] [\fB\-\-not\-before\fR] [\fB\-\-operation\-id\fR] [\fB\-o\fR|\fB\-\-output\fR] [\fB\-\-json\fR] [\fB\-\-control\fR] [\fB\-\-config\fR] [\fB\-\-context\fR] [\fB\-\-tls\-dir\fR] [\fB\-\-ca\fR] [\fB\-\-cert\fR] [\fB\-\-key\fR] [\fB\-\-as\fR] [\fB\-\-insecure\-plaintext\fR] [\fB\-\-token\fR] [\fB\-\-token\-file\fR] [\fB\-\-agent\fR] [\fB\-\-log\-format\fR] [\fB\-q\fR|\fB\-\-quiet\fR] [\fB\-\-color\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] <\fICHILD_ID\fR> 
.SH DESCRIPTION
Asks the control plane for a delegated agent\*(Aqs token, as its parent
.PP
The parent is the child\*(Aqs ID less its last segment, `42` for `42.c7`, and must have an identity here. The child gets a narrower, shorter\-lived token, recorded by the control plane, and an identity of its own that holds only that token: it connects with its root agent\*(Aqs certificate. Every node must report the `delegation` feature.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-scope\fR \fI<SCOPE>\fR
A scope the child gets instead of the defaults

`<action>:<pattern>`. Each must be covered whole by the parent\*(Aqs scopes and its `grant` patterns, and stay inside the root\*(Aqs databases, with any `grant` only below the child. Without it, the child gets the parent\*(Aqs own actions on `agent\-<child\-id>\-*`, among `admin` and `stream`, and no `grant`. Repeat it for more.
.TP
\fB\-\-ttl\fR \fI<TTL>\fR
How long the child\*(Aqs token lasts: `<n>h`, `<n>m`, or `<n>s`

From 1 minute to 24 hours. Without it, 2 hours, or less if the parent\*(Aqs token ends sooner, and the result says so. One past the parent\*(Aqs token is refused, never capped.
.TP
\fB\-\-not\-before\fR \fI<TIME>\fR
When the child\*(Aqs token starts, RFC 3339

At most 30 seconds ago, and at most 24 hours ahead; by default, now.
.TP
\fB\-\-operation\-id\fR \fI<ID>\fR
Asks under this operation ID instead of a new one

26 lowercase base32 characters, as an earlier run printed it. The same ID with another child, other scopes, another `\-\-ttl`, or another `\-\-not\-before` is refused, naming the flag.
.TP
\fB\-o\fR, \fB\-\-output\fR \fI<OUTPUT>\fR [default: table]
The output format: `table`, `json`, or `jsonl`

`table` is for people; `json` is one object with stable snake_case fields; `jsonl` is the same object on one line. A watch prints one object per line for either.
.br

.br
\fIPossible values:\fR
.RS 14
.IP \(bu 2
table: For people: a table, or key and value lines for one item
.IP \(bu 2
json: For programs: one JSON object, indented
.IP \(bu 2
jsonl: For programs: one JSON object per line
.RE
.TP
\fB\-\-json\fR
Short for `\-o json`
.TP
\fB\-\-control\fR \fI<CONTROL>\fR
The control node\*(Aqs address, `host:port`

The node that runs the control role, not any node in the fleet; a data\-only node answers with the control node\*(Aqs address. Defaults to `FLEETRING_CONTROL`, or else the context\*(Aqs `control`, when neither this nor `\-\-config` is given.
.TP
\fB\-\-config\fR \fI<CONFIG>\fR
A daemon\*(Aqs configuration file, to take the control node\*(Aqs address from
.TP
\fB\-\-context\fR \fI<NAME>\fR
Uses this context for every setting it names, instead of the current one

It outranks the environment variables; `FLEETRING_CONTEXT`, and else the current context, rank below them.
.TP
\fB\-\-tls\-dir\fR \fI<DIR>\fR
A directory with `ca.crt` and the client certificates `cert client` writes

`client.crt` and `client.key`, and the `client.<principal>.crt` and `.key` files `\-\-as` picks from. Defaults to `FLEETRING_TLS_DIR`, or else the context\*(Aqs `tls_dir`.
.TP
\fB\-\-ca\fR \fI<CA>\fR
The trusted authority certificates, PEM

Defaults to `FLEETRING_CA`, the context\*(Aqs `ca`, or `ca.crt` in the TLS directory.
.TP
\fB\-\-cert\fR \fI<CERT>\fR
The client certificate, PEM; overrides `\-\-as`

Defaults to `FLEETRING_CERT`, the context\*(Aqs `cert`, or `client.crt` in the TLS directory.
.TP
\fB\-\-key\fR \fI<KEY>\fR
The client certificate\*(Aqs private key, PEM; overrides `\-\-as`

Defaults to `FLEETRING_KEY`, the context\*(Aqs `key`, or `client.key` in the TLS directory.
.TP
\fB\-\-as\fR \fI<PRINCIPAL>\fR
Acts as this principal, with its certificate in the TLS directory

Uses `client.<principal>.crt` and `client.<principal>.key` under the TLS directory, as `cert client <principal>` writes them. An explicit certificate or key at the same step wins over this for that file, and this wins over `client.crt` and `client.key`. Defaults to `FLEETRING_AS`, or else the context\*(Aqs `as`.
.TP
\fB\-\-insecure\-plaintext\fR
Connects in plaintext, to a daemon started with `\-\-insecure\-plaintext`
.TP
\fB\-\-token\fR \fI<TOKEN>\fR
A bearer token from `token issue`, sent with every request

The request then acts with the token\*(Aqs scopes. Defaults to `FLEETRING_TOKEN`, if set.
.TP
\fB\-\-token\-file\fR \fI<PATH>\fR
A file that holds a bearer token, or `\-` for stdin

Defaults to `FLEETRING_TOKEN_FILE`, or else the context\*(Aqs `token_file`.
.TP
\fB\-\-agent\fR \fI<ID>\fR
Acts as the agent with this ID, with the identity minted for it

The identity `fleetring agent add` or `fleetring mcp \-\-agent` minted: `agent\-<id>`, its certificate, and its token, from its directory under the context\*(Aqs agents directory. A delegated agent\*(Aqs ID, such as `42.c7`, uses its root agent\*(Aqs certificate, `agent\-42`\*(Aqs, with the token `fleetring agent delegate` wrote for it. Defaults to `FLEETRING_AGENT`.
.TP
\fB\-\-log\-format\fR \fI<LOG_FORMAT>\fR
Writes log lines as `text` or `json`

Overrides `FLEETRING_LOG_FORMAT` and the configuration file\*(Aqs `[log] format`.
.TP
\fB\-q\fR, \fB\-\-quiet\fR
Prints the result and errors only

No progress, notes, warnings or override warnings. A command with no result then prints nothing.
.TP
\fB\-\-color\fR \fI<COLOR>\fR [default: auto]
When to colour log lines and the picker

`auto` colours on a terminal unless `NO_COLOR` is set or `TERM` is `dumb`; `always` and `never` do as they say.
.br

.br
\fIPossible values:\fR
.RS 14
.IP \(bu 2
auto: On a terminal, unless `NO_COLOR` is set or `TERM` is `dumb`
.IP \(bu 2
always: Always, even into a pipe or a file
.IP \(bu 2
never: Never
.RE
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help (see a summary with \*(Aq\-h\*(Aq)
.TP
<\fICHILD_ID\fR>
The child\*(Aqs ID: its parent\*(Aqs followed by `.<segment>`, such as `42.c7`

The segment is 1 to 32 lowercase letters, digits, or \*(Aq_\*(Aq. The child\*(Aqs principal, `agent\-<id>`, is at most 64 bytes, at most 8 levels below the root.
.SH EXTRA
Examples:
  fleetring agent delegate 42.c7                                   a child with the parent\*(Aqs actions on agent\-42.c7\-*
  fleetring agent delegate 42.c7 \-\-scope admin:agent\-42.c7\-* \\
      \-\-scope fork:agent\-42\-memory                                 a child that may fork the parent\*(Aqs memory
  fleetring db create agent\-42.c7\-scratch \-\-agent 42.c7            act as the child
  fleetring agent remove 42.c7                                     revoke the child and every agent below it

The command writes the operation ID into the child\*(Aqs directory before it asks, and sends the
same request again under it, up to 5 times within 60 seconds, while the control plane is
unavailable or the reply is lost. Run it again after a crash or an exit code of 4: it finds the
operation ID and resends it, and never records a second delegation.

Exit codes: 0 on success; 1 when refused for any reason but scope; 2 for usage; 3 for a refused
scope; 4 when the control plane stays unavailable after the resends.
